        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 必须",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "必须 — bìxū — \"must; it is required that\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "上课的时候必须关手机 shàngkè de shíhou bìxū guān shǒujī — You have to switch your phone off in class."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 须 (xū) — nine strokes in two pieces: on the left three left-falling strokes, one under another; on the right the page piece of 题, six strokes. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "必须 (bìxū) is built from 必 'surely' and xū, both inherited from Middle Chinese, pjit and sju (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'certain' and the second 'what the mind wants' and, quoting an older dictionary, 'the hair of the face'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
